  "rationale": "All 20 candidates are concept-aligned to basal cell carcinoma (trait_reported/trait_efo), but endpoint fidelity varies: most Cancer PRSweb models have phenotyping_reported=\"Basal cell carcinoma\" with basic covariates (age/sex/batch/PCs), whereas newer 2023 models (PGS003416/PGS003417) list phenotyping_reported=\"Keratinocyte cancers\" (broader) and the 2025 model (PGS005207) targets childhood cancer survivors (restricted endpoint with treatment-exposure covariates), so both are down-ranked for a generic basal cell carcinoma target. Within the coherent Cancer PRSweb direct-endpoint cluster, PGS000452 is best supported by the reported validation metrics: it has the highest full-model AUROC among the PRSweb set (0.632; 95% CI 0.616–0.647) and the largest reported Nagelkerke R² (0.0487) with an OR per SD of 1.663 (1.57–1.761), under comparable basic covariate adjustment. Near-ties exist (e.g., PGS000454 AUROC 0.632, R² 0.0489; PGS000456 AUROC 0.63), and none report PRS-only AUROC/R² (so full-model metrics may be partly covariate-driven), which limits certainty—hence Moderate rather than High confidence."
}

