  "rationale": "All 20 candidates are direct concept matches on trait_reported/trait_efo (basal cell carcinoma). Endpoint fidelity is strongest for models whose phenotyping_reported is explicitly “Basal cell carcinoma” (e.g., PGS000119 and the Cancer PRSweb family PGS000445–PGS000459) and weaker for restricted/special-population endpoints (PGS005207: childhood cancer survivors) or broadened/shifted phenotyping (“Keratinocyte cancers” for PGS003416/PGS003417, and “Basal cell carcinoma (MTAG)” for PGS003416). Among the endpoint-faithful candidates, PGS000119 has the best supported discrimination evidence in the provided metadata: it reports a European evaluation AUROC of 0.64 (0.62–0.66) with only basic covariates (age, sex, batch, PC1-4). Competing Cancer PRSweb siblings report lower full-model AUROCs (best ~0.632) and similar covariate sets, while the newer 2023/2025 models lack comparable AUROC/R2 (only per-SD ORs are shown). Main limitation: the selection relies on full-model AUROC (no PGS-only AUROC/R2 shown across candidates), and multiple close competitors exist (notably PGS000452/PGS000454 with AUROC 0.632), so the margin is modest and confidence is not high."
}

