  "outcome": "DIRECT_SUB_OPTIMAL",
  "best_model_id": "PGS003428",
  "confidence": "Moderate",
  "rationale": "All 6 candidates are direct matches (trait_efo=cervical carcinoma; phenotyping_reported is cervical cancer/incident cervical cancer). PGS003428 is preferred because it comes from a cervical-phenotype-focused GWAS meta-analysis paper (“GWAS meta-analyses clarify genetics of cervical phenotypes and inform risk stratification for cervical cancer”) and uses a genome-wide LDpred construction (2,894,555 variants) with a direct incident cervical cancer endpoint and relatively simple covariates (age, smoking), plus an explicit per-SD effect size (HR=1.33). Competing models are either cross-cancer/risk-factor-integration near-clones built from a very small GWS SNP set (PGS000073/PGS000784; full-model AUROC~0.745 but with several reproductive/behavior covariates, making PRS contribution less separable) or pan-trait UKB framework (PGS001299, snpnet) or show weaker discrimination in the reported full-model metric (PGS003389 C-index=0.563; PGS005165 C-index=0.566 in EAS only). Confidence is not High because most candidates lack clearly comparable PRS-only metrics, and the AUROC/C-index values reported are largely full-model and not directly comparable across differing covariate sets and study designs."
